CHCrossword
Copyright 2026 bateske

From CHBlackjack (https://github.com/bateske/CHBlackjack, Apache-2.0), by way
of CHChess and CHBackgammon: the input and frame pacing (src/CHGame.*),
palette, drawing, outlined lettering, effects, sound sequencer, flash saving,
debug protocol and the PC simulator and tools, adapted here; CHChess's
pointing glove (tools/art/hand.png) and CHBackgammon's display font
(tools/art/font.txt). CHBlackjack is a derivative of "Blackjack" for the
Arduboy by Press Play On Tape (Apache-2.0); the 3x5 pixel font in
src/gfx/Draw.cpp is Press Play On Tape's.

The close-up's letters (tools/art/tilefont.txt) are rasterized from DejaVu
Serif Bold by tools/tilefont.py. DejaVu is freely redistributable: Bitstream
Vera Fonts Copyright (c) 2003 Bitstream, Inc.; DejaVu changes are in the
public domain (https://dejavu-fonts.github.io/License.html).

The SD card block driver and FAT reader (src/sd, and the simulator's card
in tools/chsim/host/sd_host.cpp and VCard.h) are CHSd, the library this
game shares with CHWords and CHWordWheel: HypeRunner's (MIT, clean-room
from the SD and FAT specifications), polled and read-only. The FAT image
builder the tests and the simulator's card use (tools/puzzles/fatimg.py) is
HypeRunner's too, by way of CHSd.

The grid maker (tools/puzzles/fill.py) chooses words from the ENABLE word
list (public domain), keeping to common ones by the word frequencies of the
wordfreq package (Robyn Speer; its data is CC BY-SA 4.0). Neither is part of
the game: they are build-time aids. The puzzles' grids were filled with the
grid maker and their clues written for this game.

Everything else - the puzzles, their format and tools, the rules, the score
and the presentation - is new, under the Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE).
